controls.title:
SWEEP — which parameter of the system being swept is the x axis of the diagram;
each column integrates the system fresh at that value and plots the maxima of z.
The system is the most recent flow mode.

Built-in solids — the rack modules and the 19-inch frame at their real dimensions, the geometry as closed solids, and every attractor swept as a tube along its own trajectory.
Generated in the browser;
the same models are written as .stl files by chaosrack stlgen.

OPAC — every terminal's background opacity, in percent: the setting a translucent terminal emulator has (kitty's background_opacity, alacritty's window.opacity), never something a program asks for.
It applies to the default background, which is black;
text stays opaque.
At 0 only the text is there;
higher, each sheet darkens what is behind it, so the far side is dimmer than the near.

Physics — the figure as a rigid body in the plane of the screen, inside a room whose walls are the edges of the picture.
Its positions stand in the model bank after the Turtle Path's constants (Sequences).
ON (on GRAV) switches it on;
the knobs are live while it is on.
GRAV pulls either way up;
FRIC is how much the surfaces bite;
BOUNCE is how much of the speed a wall gives back;
SPIN is how hard it is to turn.

gravity — pull in world units per second squared; below zero lifts.

1.3.1 · Model — the model playing.
The outer ring picks the category and the inner ring the model in it;
OFF at the bottom of the outer ring powers the rack down, the same as the Console's Power switch, and every setting stays as it was.

